# Diff for `packages/babel-generator/src/source-map.ts`

The change modifies the logic in the `mark()` method around how it decides whether to use `originalMapping.name` versus `identifierName`. The relevant portion of the diff:

The old code checked `if (!originalMapping.name && identifierNamePos)` — meaning it only looked up the name when no original name existed. A comment in the original explained the intent, noting that if a name was found, "nothing else needs to be done".

The new code replaces this with a branch that **prefers** the original name from the input sourcemap. The added logic (verbatim from the diff):

```ts
        // Prefer the original name from the input sourcemap when marking an
        // identifier token at the same column, or when marking a related
        // token such as `(` via identifierNamePos.
        if (
          originalMapping.name &&
          (identifierNamePos ||
            (identifierName != null && originalMapping.column === column))
        ) {
          identifierName = originalMapping.name;
        } else if (identifierNamePos) {
          // Maybe we're marking a `(` and the input map already had a name attached there,
          // or we're marking a `(` and the sourcemap spanned a `foo(`,
          // or we're marking an identifier, etc.
          // We're trying to mark a `(` (as that's the only thing that provides
          // an identifierNamePos currently), and we the AST had an identifier attached.
          // Lookup it's original name.
```

The diff context ends there (the full body of the `else if` branch is not shown in the provided content).

