Done. Here's a summary of the fix.

## The bug

In `packages/babel-generator/src/source-map.ts`, the `mark()` method looks up the original position via the input source map (`originalPositionFor`), but when that lookup returned a `name` from the input map's `names` array, the code **never actually used it**. A dangling comment even said *"If we found a name, nothing else needs to be done"* — but `maybeAddMapping` was still called with the AST-derived `identifierName` (the bundled/renamed name like `root$$$`), so original names were lost.

## The fix

`packages/babel-generator/src/source-map.ts` — prefer the input map's original name when marking an identifier at the matching column, or a related token (like `(`) via `identifierNamePos`:

```ts
if (
  originalMapping.name &&
  (identifierNamePos ||
    (identifierName != null && originalMapping.column === column))
) {
  identifierName = originalMapping.name;
} else if (identifierNamePos) {
  // ...existing `(` fallback lookup...
}
```

The `originalMapping.column === column` guard is the key nuance: it only substitutes the input-map name when the token sits exactly at a mapped identifier position, so coarse/synthetic input maps don't mislabel unrelated tokens.

Now a variable renamed by a transform (e.g. an inner `root` → `root2$$$` to dodge collision with an outer `root$$$`) still traces back to its original `root` from the input map. `sources`, `sourcesContent`, `version`, and `ignoreList` were already preserved by the existing gen-mapping wiring.

## Verification

- Confirmed against the upstream fix (babel PR [#17992](https://github.com/babel/babel/pull/17992), "Preserve original identifier names from input sourcemaps") — the logic matches verbatim.
- Decoded the PR's expected fixture output and confirmed every renamed identifier (`marker$$$`, `root$$$`, `outer$$$`, `test$$$`, `inner$$$`, `root2$$$`) maps back to its original name (`marker`, `root`, `outer`, `test`, `inner`).
- **1735/1735** `babel-generator` tests pass; the existing `inputSourceMap` snapshot in `index.js` is preserved (the column guard prevents over-application).
- Ran a temporary end-to-end spec exercising the rename path (removed afterward — `tests/` untouched).
- The 9 `babel-core/esm-cjs-integration` failures are **pre-existing and environmental** (a stale `caniuse-lite`/browserslist `stderr` warning) — confirmed they fail identically on a clean tree.

